 "stem": "Find the expansion of $({=p}x-{=q}y)^5$.",
 "answer": "{=c0}x^5 - {=c1}x^4y + {=c2}x^3y^2 - {=c3}x^2y^3 + {=c4}xy^4 - {=c5}y^5",
 "solution": [
  "$({=p}x-{=q}y)^5 = {}^5C_0 ({=p}x)^5 + {}^5C_1 ({=p}x)^4(-{=q}y) + {}^5C_2 ({=p}x)^3(-{=q}y)^2 + {}^5C_3 ({=p}x)^2(-{=q}y)^3 + {}^5C_4 ({=p}x)(-{=q}y)^4 + {}^5C_5 (-{=q}y)^5$.",
  "The combinations are 1, 5, 10, 10, 5, 1.",
  "Terms: ${=c0}x^5$; $5\\cdot{=p**4}\\cdot{=q} = {=c1}$; $10\\cdot{=p**3}\\cdot{=q**2} = {=c2}$; $10\\cdot{=p**2}\\cdot{=q**3} = {=c3}$; $5\\cdot{=p}\\cdot{=q**4} = {=c4}$; ${=q}^5 = {=c5}$. The signs alternate because $-{=q}y$ is raised to odd and even powers.",
  "The expansion is ${=c0}x^5 - {=c1}x^4y + {=c2}x^3y^2 - {=c3}x^2y^3 + {=c4}xy^4 - {=c5}y^5$."
 ],
